  "reason": "The current best is config_032 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) at 0.688 accuracy. The RNA side is well-optimized, but the image modality is the weakest link: image-only ResNet50 scored only 0.208, suggesting poor image representation may be limiting the multimodal gain (only +3.5% over RNA-only). Config_038 changes exactly one variable—swapping ResNet50 for imagenet_vit_l—while keeping the proven scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer aggregation, and concat fusion. This cleanly isolates whether a stronger, pretrained ViT-L image encoder can unlock additional multimodal benefit. With 2 experiments remaining, this high-leverage test of image representation quality is the best use of the next slot: if ViT-L helps, we can exploit further; if not, we confirm the image modality's ceiling and can pivot to fusion-method refinement (config_033) in the final experiment."
}

